# Layer A density v4 fixture: 25-option-some-unwrap with SCS caseType
# inference.
#
# v4 vs v3:
#   - The `someCase SCS "Some" intT` declaration elides the caseType
#     (uses `_`). The elaborator infers `intT` by walking SV nodes that
#     supply payloads for this case and resolving their payload types.
#     `someValue SV optionT "Some" 42` has an inline IntLit payload
#     whose type resolves to `intT` via the implicit prelude, so the
#     SCS's caseType is inferred as `intT`.
#
# Round-trip: canonical hash equals 25-option-some-unwrap.json's.
@v=1 root=result
someCase SCS "Some" _
noneCase SCS "None" _
optionT SUM [someCase noneCase]
someValue SV optionT "Some" 42
result WHEN someValue optionT "Some(n) -> n | None -> 0"
